                                    <div class="faq-section" style="margin-top:40px;">
                                        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
                                        <h3>What makes ayurveda skincare different from generic skincare?</h3>
                                        <p>Heritage-storytelling + ingredient sourcing transparency + apothecary sensory packaging + Ayurveda-doctor endorsement + PR + heritage-publication placements + regional heritage sensitivity + long-cycle brand-building. Different funnel + creative + content.</p>
                                        <h3>Should we hire ayurveda specialist or category-broad agency?</h3>
                                        <p>Specialist for premium heritage-designer brands (Rs 5+ Cr revenue) with luxury + celebrity + Vogue-tier ambition. Category-broad with proven ayurveda track record for most launches. Generic beauty almost always wrong for heritage ayurveda.</p>
                                        <h3>What agency capabilities matter for ayurveda skincare?</h3>
                                        <p>Heritage-storytelling + PR + Vogue-tier publication + ingredient-sourcing transparency + apothecary packaging + ayurveda-doctor sourcing + regional-heritage sensitivity + long-cycle brand-building comfort + sensory + gifting + luxury-adjacent campaign design.</p>
                                        <h3>What is a realistic ayurveda D2C launch envelope?</h3>
                                        <p>Rs 40-90 lakh capex + first-6-month operating. Higher inventory + ingredient sourcing + brand + packaging + PR + heritage-publication investment. Rs 25L/month by month 12-18. Rs 1 Cr/month within 30-40 months for top-quartile.</p>
                                        <h3>What ayurveda + heritage positioning works?</h3>
                                        <p>Kama Ayurveda (premium heritage), Forest Essentials (luxury heritage), Just Herbs (herbal science + heritage), Juicy Chemistry (ayurveda + clean beauty hybrid). Pick ONE + own it year 1. Requires genuine ingredient / heritage / craft story.</p>
                                        <h3>Where does ITD sit in ayurveda skincare agency landscape?</h3>
                                        <p>Category-broad D2C with proven ayurveda vertical: Ayurveda D2C Playbook + Kama Ayurveda Case Study + Best D2C Ayurveda Brands playbook + Best Marketing Agency Ayurveda D2C Brands published. Heritage-storytelling + PR + ingredient sourcing + long-cycle brand-building fluency.</p>
